\par

\b Testing horizon and decision gates\b0
\par
- Phase 1 (1-2 weeks): pipeline stability and settlement correctness.
\par
- Phase 2 (6-8 weeks): early directional read from CLV and settled outcomes.
\par
- Phase 3 (4-6 months): medium confidence ROI read (target roughly 250-400 settled bets).
\par
- Phase 4 (9-12 months): high-confidence performance read (target 500+ settled bets).
\par
- Use CLV earlier as a faster signal; use settled ROI over longer windows to avoid noise.
\par

\b What I need you to do\b0
\par
- Use this model and codebase to propose and, where possible, implement changes that make it more robust and higher-ROI.
\par
- Apply the standards you would use in a professional trading environment: calibration, edge by segment, risk control, and repeatability.
\par
- Aim for a transformed setup that you would be willing to run with real capital: robust, well-calibrated, and targeting high ROI.
\par
- You can act as senior analyst, quant, or model lead; the bar is institutional-grade transformation of our current model.
\par
- Respect the policy lock (docs/FAIR-ODDS-POLICY-LOCK.md): any model or policy change requires explicit approval, backtest comparison vs locked baseline, rolling year-slice checks, and a note in the lock document.
\par
